# chktex configuration for tex-thesis
# See: https://www.nongnu.org/chktex/ChkTeX.pdf

# Suppress warnings that conflict with our formatting:
# 1  - Command terminated with space (common with \item, etc.)
# 2  - Non-breaking space before \cite/\ref (noisy, style preference)
# 3  - Enclose previous parenthesis with {}  (false positives in math)
# 8  - Wrong length of dash (we handle intentionally via literate)
# 9  - `}' expected, found `)' (false positive in \labelenumi definitions)
# 10 - Solo `}' found (false positive in \labelenumi definitions)
# 12 - Interword spacing (false positive with abbreviations like "et al.")
# 13 - Intersentence spacing (false positive with abbreviations like "CPU:")
# 17 - Number of `(' doesn't match `)' (false positive from complex macros)
# 24 - Delete from/to `}' (false positive with \makeatother blocks)
# 36 - Vertical rules in tables (we use them intentionally for academic style)
# 44 - User Regex (not configured)
CmdLine {
    --nowarn 1
    --nowarn 2
    --nowarn 3
    --nowarn 8
    --nowarn 9
    --nowarn 10
    --nowarn 12
    --nowarn 13
    --nowarn 17
    --nowarn 24
    --nowarn 36
    --nowarn 44
}

# Environments to ignore (code listings, tikzpicture, etc.)
VerbEnvir {
    lstlisting
    verbatim
    tikzpicture
}
